Subject: m68k EMAC: specialise the fractional mode at translation time

RT and OMC are already TB flags (cpu_get_tb_cpu_state takes MACSR bits 7..4),
yet the inline fractional MAC and get_macf re-read them from MACSR at run
time. Decide them when translating: no rounding code when RT = 0, the
saturation select without the OMC test. MACSR N, Z, V, EV are skipped for a
MAC whose next instruction, in the same TB with nothing that can observe the
state in between, is another MAC or move-to-ACC (they clear and recompute all
four; the sticky PAV bits are still accumulated). move.l <ea>,ACCx computes
its flags inline in the fractional mode instead of calling
helper_mac_set_flags, and not at all under the same condition.

